      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Mo and W to a titanium- and nickel-primary high-entropy alloy will improve its elevated-temperature mechanical properties.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial material is a high-entropy alloy in which both Ti and Ni are primary constituents.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A high-entropy alloy can be defined as containing at least five elements at 5–35 at% each with similar atomic radii.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9571103::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant operating regime is above 1000°C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Mo and W will produce a single-phase solid solution in the proposed alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9571103::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting single-phase solid solution will have either an FCC or BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9571103::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo and W additions will enhance solid-solution strengthening in the proposed alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced solid-solution strengthening will improve mechanical properties at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have greater elevated-temperature strength than the alloy without refractory-element additions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC8074761::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have greater hardness at elevated temperature than the alloy without refractory-element additions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have greater oxidation resistance at elevated temperature than the alloy without refractory-element additions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have greater corrosion resistance at elevated temperature than the alloy without refractory-element additions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
